        "steps": [
            {
                "recipe_order": null,
                "step": "Put a layer about 1 cm deep of air-dried, sieved good calcareous garden loam into a\r\ntest tube or jar. (The use of mud from rivers or ponds is rarely satisfactory.)\r\nCarefully add deionised water to a depth of 7 to 10 cm, plug or cover, and steam\r\nfor one hour or autoclave for 15 minutes at 15 psi (longer for larger vessels) on\r\neach of 2 consecutive days; further sterilisation is not needed. Allow to stand for a\r\nfurther day before inoculating, when the pH should be between 7.0 - 8.0."
            },
            {
                "recipe_order": null,
                "step": "S/W is  prepared  as  above,  but approximately  0.01  g  ammonium  magnesium \r\nphosphate is placed into the base of the test tube before adding the soil and water."
            }
        ],
        "equipment": []
    }
